  "body": " Which pins can TIM14 drive?   Which timer a pin can carry, and under which alternate function, is a property of the STM32C031C6 chip, so it is in the chip's datasheet : Table 12, Pin assignment and description , on page 30 names the functions, and the alternate-function tables on pages 36 to 39 give the AF number. Which chip pin is at which position on the Arduino header is a property of the Nucleo board, and that is the Nucleo pinout.     TIM14 has one PWM output, its channel 1, named TIM14_CH1 in the datasheet, and the chip can route that output to any of several pins. Fill in the table: every pin that can carry TIM14_CH1, the alternate function (AF) number it is under, and, if the pin reaches the Arduino header, its name there. Table 12 of the STM32C031C6 datasheet, Pin assignment and description , page 30, names the functions; the alternate-function tables on pages 36 to 39 give the AF number.       Pin  AF  Arduino header name, if any                                                                        One of them carried the motor's PWM in the motor chapter. Which is it, what is its name on the Arduino header, and what does choosing it save us today?   "
